{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '107,127p' docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md; rg 'StrictMode|Fast Refresh' -n node_modules/react-dom/cjs/react-dom-client.development.js | head -12; rg -n 'forwardRef\\\\(|\\\\.getOwnPropertyDescriptor|ref.*render' node_modules/react/cjs/react.development.js | tail -25; cat packages/axylo/dist/index.d.ts | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\n\n```ts\nchart.update({ title: 'Sessions' });                 // options\nchart.append([{ day: '2026-05-01', channel: 'Direct', sessions: 41210 }], { keep: 120 });   // rows\nchart.zoom(['2026-03-01', '2026-03-31']);            // view\nconst off = chart.on('hover', point => { … });\nchart.diagnostics;                                   // current, as soon as any call returns\nchart.destroy();\n```\n\nFinding D3: the ten libraries have seven update idioms. Axylo has three methods, one per kind of change, with one contract.\n\n| Rule | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Order | Calls are applied in the order made. `update({ data })` followed by `append` appends to the new data. |\n| Two phases | Each call validates and normalizes synchronously: diagnostics are current when it returns, and a `strict` chart throws from that call. Drawing is deferred to the next animation frame, and calls made before that frame are drawn once. |\n| Atomic switch | Marks, labels, hit testing and the accessibility layer move to a new data revision together. No frame mixes two revisions. |\n| Patches | A key present in an `update` replaces the old value whole; a key set to `undefined` returns to its default; absent keys stay. No deep merging. |\n| Rejected changes | A call that throws under `strict` leaves the chart on its last valid state. |\n| Streaming | `keep` is the number of distinct x values retained. Rows before the last x are accepted through the slower full update and raise AX151. While zoomed to the latest edge the view follows new data; zoomed elsewhere, it stays put. Paused charts buffer (I6). Keyboard focus stays on its datum until that datum leaves the window (A7). |\n409:          return \"StrictMode\";\n498:          return type === REACT_STRICT_MODE_TYPE ? \"StrictMode\" : \"Mode\";\n1131:    function setIsStrictModeForDevtools(newIsStrictMode) {\n1133:        unstable_setDisableYieldValue(newIsStrictMode);\n1134:      if (injectedHook && \"function\" === typeof injectedHook.setStrictMode)\n1136:          injectedHook.setStrictMode(rendererID, newIsStrictMode);\n7691:                      setIsStrictModeForDevtools(!0);\n7695:                        setIsStrictModeForDevtools(!1);\n7716:                      setIsStrictModeForDevtools(!0);\n7720:                        setIsStrictModeForDevtools(!1);\n8040:        setIsStrictModeForDevtools(!0);\n8049:          setIsStrictModeForDevtools(!1);\n172:        var getter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(config, \"key\").get;\n1021:            (JSCompiler_inline_result = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(\n1148:            \"forwardRef requires a render function but received a `memo` component. Instead of forwardRef(memo(...)), use memo(forwardRef(...)).\"\n/**\n * Axylo's public entry points. Importing this module touches no DOM, so it loads in Node, where `validate`\n * runs; the chart functions need a document and are only called in a browser.\n */\nimport type { AreaOptions, BarOptions, Chart, Diagnostic, DonutOptions, LineOptions, ScatterOptions, Target } from './public';\nexport type * from './public';\nexport declare function line<Row>(target: Target, options: LineOptions<Row>): Chart<Row, LineOptions<Row>>;\nexport declare function area<Row>(target: Target, options: AreaOptions<Row>): Chart<Row, AreaOptions<Row>>;\nexport declare function bar<Row>(target: Target, options: BarOptions<Row>): Chart<Row, BarOptions<Row>>;\nexport declare function scatter<Row>(target: Target, options: ScatterOptions<Row>): Chart<Row, ScatterOptions<Row>>;\nexport declare function donut<Row>(target: Target, options: DonutOptions<Row>): Chart<Row, DonutOptions<Row>>;\n/** Runs option resolution and normalization only, without a DOM, and returns the diagnostics (plan 1.6). */\nexport declare function validate<Row>(type: 'line' | 'area' | 'bar', options: LineOptions<Row> | AreaOptions<Row> | BarOptions<Row>): Diagnostic[];\nexport declare function validate<Row>(type: 'scatter', options: ScatterOptions<Row>): Diagnostic[];\nexport declare function validate<Row>(type: 'donut', options: DonutOptions<Row>): Diagnostic[];\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
